cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: "MuViSeg: Multi-View Segment Correspondences from Dense Geometry Priors"
abstract: >-
  Given several images of the same scene and class-agnostic segmentation masks
  for each, MuViSeg predicts which segments correspond to the same physical
  object. A frozen 3D foundation-model backbone (MASt3R or VGGT) supplies dense
  descriptors, masked average pooling yields one descriptor per segment, and a
  lightweight trainable head predicts the assignment with a dustbin for
  unmatched segments.
